    "goal": "Seed HepG2 cells in a 96-well plate at a moderate growth-phase seeding density of 1e4 cells/cm^2 and determine the standard working medium volume per well.",
    "rationale": "HepG2 is a liver cell line with a doubling time of ~48-60 h. A moderate growth-phase seeding density of 1e4 cells/cm^2 is within the lower end of the HepG2 growth-phase range (2e4-6.3e4 cells/cm^2 per the registry), giving cells room to expand over several days before confluence. The 96-well plate has a growth area of ~0.32 cm^2, so 1e4 cells/cm^2 yields 3,200 cells/well. Standard working medium volume for a 96-well plate is 0.17 mL/well (Corning/Falcon recommended).",
